## What I plan to add next

## Better Database
Right now the app uses SQLite which works great for one person. If thousands of people use this app at the same time, I would switch to PostgreSQL which is built to handle many users simultaneously without slowing down.

## Cloud Image Storage
Currently clothing images are saved on the server's local storage. For a real deployed app, I would move images to AWS S3 or Cloudinary — this way images load faster from anywhere in the world and don't get lost if the server restarts.

## Mobile App
The web app already works on mobile browsers, but a dedicated mobile app built with React Native would give a much better experience — faster loading, camera access to directly photograph clothes, and push notifications for daily outfit reminders.

## Social Features
Users could share their outfit combinations with friends, follow other users for style inspiration, and rate each other's outfits. Think of it like Instagram but specifically for fashion and outfits.

## Virtual Try-On
Upload your photo and see how an outfit actually looks on you before wearing it — using AI image generation.

## Price Tracker
Add the price of each clothing item when uploading. The app tracks how many times you wear each item and calculates cost-per-wear — helping you make smarter shopping decisions.